# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the Python version is
#   checked in a different way. Clear the comment if you want to use it.
#.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1180, pipenv manages the virtual environment in a central location.
#   Therefore, if you wish to lock the dependencies for your project, you should commit
#   Pipfile.lock to your repository.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to pipenv, poetry manages python virtual environments and dependencies.
#   You should commit poetry.lock to your repository.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to pipenv and poetry, pdm manages python virtual environments and dependencies.
#   You should commit pdm.lock to your repository.
#pdm.lock

# PEP 582 spaces
__pypackages__/

